  "title": "India's Sugar Stock Limits and Price Trends",
  "summary": "India's government has tightened sugar stock limits to manage domestic prices, while festive demand has driven up prices, with dealers holding sugar for only 15 days. The new season sets a base price for sugarcane at ₹365 per quintal for the 2026-27 season.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India's government allows duty-free import of 10 lakh tonnes of raw sugar until October 31, aiming to control domestic prices.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dealers hold sugar for only 15 days from October 15 to November 30, with Kolkata and its extended metropolitan areas having a 2,000-quintal limit.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The new season begins on October 1, with the FRP for sugarcane set at ₹365 per quintal for the 2026-27 season.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
